   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "one scale per (64, d) tile of Q and per (64, d) tile of K, stored as two small FP32 arrays (B, N/64).\nIn the kernel the score tile for (Q tile i, KV tile j) is multiplied by s_q[i] s_k[j] / sqrt(d): one scalar\nread per iteration, served from L1 after the first thread. V keeps one scale per tensor.\nA single outlier can now only coarsen its own 64-row block instead of the whole tensor.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "one scale per (64, d) tile of Q and per (64, d) tile of K, stored as two small FP32 arrays (B, N/64).\nIn the kernel the score tile for (Q tile i, KV tile j) is multiplied by s_q[i] s_k[j] / sqrt(d): one scalar\nread per iteration, served from L1 after the first thread. V keeps one scale per tensor.\nA single outlier can now only coarsen its own 64-row block instead of the whole tensor.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
